{
  "text": "The Carter Family, episode 37, The Airplane Trip. I can't wait to fly in an airplane, Harry said. Flying sounds scary, Oliver said. It will be fun, dad said. Lots of people got on the plane. We might be too heavy for the plane, Oliver said. We're not too heavy, mom said. The plane took off. The Carter family was flying. My ears hurt, Oliver said. Mom gave Oliver a piece of gum. Chewing the gum made his ears feel better. Oliver looked out the window. We are very high up, he said. What if we fall? Harry said, We will not fall. Mom gave the kids a card game. Oliver can go first, Emmy said. Oliver won the game. That was fun, he said. A flight attendant brought drinks and a snack. Yum, said Oliver. I love pretzels and juice. The plane landed. Everyone got their luggage. The flight attendant smiled at Oliver. Would you like to meet the pilot? She asked. Yes. Oliver said. The pilot had a cool uniform. He showed Oliver the cockpit. Oliver saw buttons and lights and maps. Wow. Oliver said. Does flying still seem scary, Oliver? Dad asked. Scary? Oliver laughed. Flying is not scary, Dad. Flying is awesome.",
